We use the shrinking window concept to get the minimum window having all three characters, then shrink the window from left while maintaing three unique characters.
## Approach
Initialize l and r equal to 0 and a totalCount also as 0. Also have a freqMap to track what characters are in the current window.

Expand the window from right and keep adding characters to the map, once the map size is three, this means we have three unique characters. Add n-r to the totalCount to cover all substrings starting from this particular substring. Now, while maintaing the map size as 3, shrink the window from left and keep updating the totalCount to get all possible substrings' count.

